# The motivating case: the eval'd code itself calls `s.complete`. `s` is captured
# from the body (call-site capture), so the nested code reaches it; the completion it
# throws propagates out through s.eval to the embedRepl boundary.
>>> {"op":"eval","code":"val r = embedRepl[Int] { s => s.eval(\"s.complete(42)\") }"}
~ "ok":true.*val r: Int = 42
